Comments: [Evaluator: Christian Iliadis; Date: 08/28/2024]
 1. A radius parameter of 0.95 fm gives a radius (R = 3.9 fm) closer to what was assumed for extracting alpha-particle spectroscopic factors in Tanabe et al. 1981
    and Madhusoodhanan et al. 1999.
 2. Er = 2767 - 3756 keV: resonance strenghs from Endt 1990.
 3. Er = 2542, 2519, 2290 keV: partial widths are deduced from experimental values of wg_pg, wg_pa, wg_ag.
 4. Er = 2078 keV: the partial widths are estimated from wg_ag, Ga/G and Gg/G (Ross et al. 1995), and Gp from (3He,d).
 5. Er = 1916 keV: Ga and Gg from Aboud et al. 2018.
 6. Er = 1745 keV: experimental strength is the average from Rogers et al. 1977 and Toevs 1971.
 7. Er = 1555 keV: partial widths are deduced from measured wg_ag and lifetime (Babilon et al. 2002).
 8. Er = 170 to 1462 keV: Gg = 0.1 eV is an inconsequential guess.
 9. Er = 489 keV: total width is found from measured lifetime; Ga is estimated from experimental transfer spectroscopic factor (Tanabe et al. 1981, Madhusoodhanan 
    et al. 1999).
10. Direct capture (E2) is estimated using alpha spectroscopic factors listed in Table 2 of Madhusoodhanan et al. (1999).
